{"review_id":"00001788303359016607-0004098830-000001-cycle-review-1","reviewed_manifest_hash":"sha256:1de7363e41457da2b5466aa2d8341f0dd752a3545c15febcec7a85ccf6fc5ea6","findings":[{"finding_id":"F1-orphan-tool-result","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"A refused/malformed tool call produces an orphan tool_result on the next turn, which the Messages API rejects","claim":"`push_assistant_and_tool_turn` emits a `tool_result` block for every `ToolResultPayload` unconditionally, but only emits the matching `tool_use` block when the call id is present in `tool_use_registry`. The adapter deliberately does not register a call whose accumulated `input_json_delta` fragments fail to parse (`if let Ok(parsed) = serde_json::from_str::<Value>(&accumulated)` in the `ContentBlockStop` arm), while the loop core still refuses that call and appends a `tool_result` message for it. On the following submission the adapter therefore builds a `user` message containing a `tool_result` with no preceding `tool_use` block (and, when the turn carried no assistant text, no `assistant` message at all, so the `tool_result` user message directly follows another user message). Anthropic's Messages API rejects both shapes with 400 `invalid_request_error`, which this adapter classifies as `NonRetryable(InvalidRequest)` — so the very path the design documents as \"refused without execution\" terminates the whole loop on the next turn rather than letting the model recover. The same hole applies to any `tool_result` whose id is not in the registry (a fresh adapter instance resuming persisted history, or an entry lost to a stream interruption). The unit test `malformed_tool_arguments_surface_as_a_fragment_never_executed_here` asserts the registry is empty for that call but never submits a follow-up turn, so nothing covers the resulting request shape.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/anthropic.rs","range":{"start":268,"end":338}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:7c07dbb21500bd3bf9ee9a0c129af5b9dbbf4442957df520daf66588b1777307","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":36688,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-59","revision":"sha256:0da5fbff2d99b77a9992e12ecc835a961996e1a1b5edcd4907f955cfb2dfa011","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-7c07dbb21500bd3bf9ee9a0c129af5b9dbbf4442957df520daf66588b1777307-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Never emit a `tool_result` block without its `tool_use` partner: when `tool_use_registry` has no entry for `payload.call_id`, synthesize the assistant `tool_use` block from the payload itself (`id = call_id`, `name = payload.capability_name`, `input = {}` or the raw unparsed fragment string) so the wire history stays well-formed for a refused or unknown call. Add a fixture that submits a second turn after a malformed tool call and asserts the outgoing `messages` array pairs every `tool_result` with a preceding `tool_use` of the same id.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F2-interrupted-stream-usage-lost","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Usage observed before a stream interruption is discarded, not preserved","claim":"Acceptance criterion 3 requires that a partial or interrupted stream preserve observed usage, and the contract document claims \"everything the observer already received before the interruption stays delivered.\" In practice the adapter's SSE closure emits `StreamEvent::UsageDelta` only for `SseEvent::MessageDelta`; `SseEvent::MessageStart` — the frame that carries `input_tokens`, `cache_read_input_tokens`, and `cache_creation_input_tokens` — falls into the closure's `_ => {}` arm, so those categories never reach any observer. When the stream then ends without a stop reason, `stream_messages` returns `Err(AdapterError::Ambiguous)` and discards the `StreamOutcome` it had already accumulated, and `run_loop` records `AttemptUsage { usage: UsageCategories::default(), ambiguous: true }`. The input and cache-read tokens the provider actually reported (and will bill) are therefore observed on the wire and then dropped entirely — neither surfaced to observers nor recorded in the PRD-051 ledger. The existing test `stream_ending_without_stop_reason_is_ambiguous` asserts only that text deltas reached the observer, so the usage loss is uncovered.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/raw_runtime.rs","hunk":"@@ -927,6 +931,7 @@ pub async fn run_loop(\n                     attempt_id,\n                     usage: UsageCategories::default(),\n                     ambiguous: true,\n+                    provider_request_id: None,\n                 });\n                 break StopReason::ProviderFailure {\n                     taxonomy: ProviderFailureTaxonomy::Ambiguous,"},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/anthropic_api.rs","range":{"start":560,"end":600}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:7c07dbb21500bd3bf9ee9a0c129af5b9dbbf4442957df520daf66588b1777307","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":36688,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-59","revision":"sha256:0da5fbff2d99b77a9992e12ecc835a961996e1a1b5edcd4907f955cfb2dfa011","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-7c07dbb21500bd3bf9ee9a0c129af5b9dbbf4442957df520daf66588b1777307-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Emit a `StreamEvent::UsageDelta` for `SseEvent::MessageStart` as well, and carry the partially accumulated `StreamOutcome` out of `stream_messages` on the ambiguous path (e.g. `AdapterError::Ambiguous { reason, observed_usage }` or an `Err` variant holding the outcome) so `run_loop` can record the observed categories alongside `ambiguous: true` instead of `UsageCategories::default()`. Extend the interrupted-stream fixture to assert the observed input/cache-read tokens survive.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F3-tool-use-registry-unbounded","category":"maintainability_issue","severity":"low","blocking":false,"title":"tool_use_registry and attempt_metadata grow without bound for the adapter's lifetime","claim":"`tool_use_registry` gains an entry for every completed `tool_use` block and is never pruned — no turn boundary, execution boundary, or `cancel` path removes entries (`cancel` clears only `attempt_metadata`, and only for the one attempt id). `attempt_metadata` likewise accumulates one entry per successful attempt with no eviction. A long-lived adapter instance shared across many executions therefore retains every tool call's name, arguments, and any preceding thinking text (including its opaque signature) for the process lifetime, which is both unbounded memory growth and a longer-than-necessary retention window for model reasoning content.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/anthropic.rs","range":{"start":100,"end":110}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/anthropic.rs","range":{"start":268,"end":338}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"lint","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:bdaf7a8bd1623527e3fb84a4a90504364a0fd9b21ab09029f97548fb9ef43c68","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":1268,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-59","revision":"sha256:0da5fbff2d99b77a9992e12ecc835a961996e1a1b5edcd4907f955cfb2dfa011","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-bdaf7a8bd1623527e3fb84a4a90504364a0fd9b21ab09029f97548fb9ef43c68-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Bound both maps: drop a registry entry once its `tool_result` has been replayed (or cap it with an LRU keyed by call id), and evict `attempt_metadata` entries after the host has read them or on `cancel`/run completion. Document the intended lifetime in the contract's replay section.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F4-paths-outside-allowed","category":"scope_violation","severity":"low","blocking":false,"title":"Change touches paths outside the task's allowed_paths (\"crates/\")","claim":"The task declares `allowed_paths: [\"crates/\"]`, but the candidate revision also modifies workspace-root `Cargo.toml` and `Cargo.lock`, `config/default.toml`, and adds/edits `docs/contracts/anthropic-adapter.md` and `docs/contracts/providers-index.md`. The edits themselves look purposeful and consistent with the objective (a new `stream` feature on `reqwest`, a new `futures-util` workspace dependency, commented-out worked configuration examples, and the normative contract document), but they fall outside the declared path allowance, which is a disposition decision rather than something this review can waive.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"Cargo.toml","range":{"start":57,"end":62}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"config/default.toml","range":{"start":36,"end":50}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"docs/contracts/providers-index.md","range":{"start":26,"end":27}}],"remediation":"Either widen the task's `allowed_paths` to cover the workspace manifest, `config/`, and `docs/contracts/` before accepting, or split the out-of-scope edits into a separately authorized change.","status":"open","supersedes":null}]}
