Summary of remediation for **F1-orphan-tool-result**:

- In `push_assistant_and_tool_turn`, when a `tool_result`'s `call_id` has no entry in `tool_use_registry` (a refused malformed call, or an id unknown to a fresh adapter instance), the adapter now synthesizes a `tool_use` block from the payload itself (`id = call_id`, `name = capability_name`, `input = {}`) instead of silently omitting it. Every `tool_result` is now guaranteed a preceding `tool_use` of the same id, and the assistant message is never empty/omitted when tool results are present.
- Added a new fixture, `refused_malformed_call_never_produces_an_orphan_tool_result_on_the_next_turn`, which streams a malformed tool call, submits a second turn carrying its refused `tool_result`, and asserts the outgoing `messages` array pairs every `tool_result` with a preceding `tool_use` of the same id (and that no `tool_result` message directly follows another user message).

Verified: `cargo test -p familiar-ai-agent anthropic` (20/20 pass), `cargo fmt --all -- --check` clean, `cargo clippy -p familiar-ai-agent --all-targets --no-default-features -- -D warnings ...` clean.
