{"review_id":"00001788303359016607-0004098830-000001-cycle-review-2","reviewed_manifest_hash":"sha256:95b50b3c9fd69d0938635bdbc1f82b983459b320d144ca21da94945b0e52b828","findings":[{"finding_id":"F2-sse-utf8-chunk-split","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"SSE byte chunks are decoded with from_utf8_lossy per chunk, corrupting multi-byte characters split across chunk boundaries","claim":"`stream_messages` accumulates the response body with `byte_buf.push_str(&String::from_utf8_lossy(&chunk))`, decoding each `bytes_stream()` chunk independently. HTTP/TLS chunk boundaries are arbitrary byte offsets and routinely split a multi-byte UTF-8 sequence; `from_utf8_lossy` then replaces the truncated tail of chunk N and the orphaned continuation bytes at the head of chunk N+1 with U+FFFD. The buffer that frames are parsed from therefore contains silently corrupted characters. This corrupts `text_delta` content surfaced to the loop and persisted as final text, and corrupts `input_json_delta` fragments: JSON structural characters are ASCII so the accumulated arguments still parse, meaning a tool call is executed with a corrupted string value (a path, a patch body, a commit message containing any non-ASCII byte) rather than being refused as malformed. Every fixture in the suite serves its SSE body as one wiremock chunk, so no test can observe this.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/anthropic_api.rs","range":{"start":516,"end":533}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:cb4b31fc03548066b1872f3d6ae44f09c4a5c620063e8c403a8f51c89763297e","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":36795,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-59","revision":"sha256:2c507eaf813c93ebc0f40d599d9dfbc25279c6444ed3d1c044fb54174f9cf6c1","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-cb4b31fc03548066b1872f3d6ae44f09c4a5c620063e8c403a8f51c89763297e-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Buffer the raw bytes (`Vec<u8>`) rather than a `String`: append each chunk to the byte buffer, split complete frames on the `\\n\\n` byte sequence, and decode only complete frames with `std::str::from_utf8` (or use an incremental UTF-8 decoder), so a partial code point stays in the buffer until its remaining bytes arrive. Add a fixture that delivers one SSE frame containing a multi-byte character across two response chunks and asserts the observed text round-trips byte-exactly.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F3-sse-error-event-ignored","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"A mid-stream SSE `error` event is parsed but discarded, downgrading a classified retryable provider error to Ambiguous","claim":"`SseEvent::Error { error: WireErrorBody }` is deserialized but marked `#[allow(dead_code)]` and falls into `apply_event`'s `_ => {}` arm; nothing in `stream_messages` inspects it. Anthropic emits `event: error` frames mid-stream after a 200 response (documented for `overloaded_error` and internal errors). When that happens no `stop_reason` is ever set, so the stream falls through to the `outcome.stop_reason.is_none()` branch and returns `AdapterError::Ambiguous`. The loop maps that to `StopReason::ProviderFailure { taxonomy: Ambiguous }` with ambiguous usage, so a provider error the response explicitly classified as retryable (and whose retryability the acceptance criteria require the caller to act on) is recorded as an unclassifiable failure instead of `Retryable(Overloaded)`. The error taxonomy fixtures only cover non-2xx HTTP statuses; no fixture streams an `error` event on a 200 response.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/anthropic_api.rs","range":{"start":336,"end":360}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e2e1c0d6b83291d99ee8fa1755f89f52efcd270089766f060699676b9551d918","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":97040,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-59","revision":"sha256:2c507eaf813c93ebc0f40d599d9dfbc25279c6444ed3d1c044fb54174f9cf6c1","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e2e1c0d6b83291d99ee8fa1755f89f52efcd270089766f060699676b9551d918-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Handle `SseEvent::Error` in the stream loop: classify `error.kind` through the same taxonomy used for HTTP bodies (`overloaded_error` -> `Retryable(Overloaded)`, `rate_limit_error` -> `Retryable(RateLimited)`, `api_error`/unknown -> `Ambiguous` when any content already streamed) and return that error instead of falling through to the generic no-stop-reason `Ambiguous`. Add a fixture streaming `{\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"type\":\"overloaded_error\",...}}` on a 200 response and assert the classified result.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F4-redacted-thinking-dropped","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"`redacted_thinking` blocks are parsed but never captured or replayed, so a thinking-enabled turn can be reconstructed without the block the provider requires back","claim":"`WireContentBlockStart::RedactedThinking { data }` exists in the wire enum, but the adapter's `ContentBlockStart` match handles only `ToolUse`, `Text`, and `Thinking`, dropping redacted blocks via `_ => {}`; nothing stores them and `RememberedToolUse.preceding_thinking` holds only `(thinking, signature)` pairs. Under the provider's replay rule (which this adapter's contract document commits to: \"Thinking blocks are replayed unchanged on the same model, per the provider's replay rules\"), redacted thinking must be passed back alongside ordinary thinking. With `thinking_enabled` set and a safety-redacted reasoning block preceding a `tool_use`, the next turn's reconstructed assistant message contains the `tool_use` block with no preceding thinking or redacted-thinking block at all, which the Messages API rejects for a thinking-enabled request — turning an ordinary tool round-trip into `NonRetryable(InvalidRequest)` that terminates the loop. No fixture streams a `redacted_thinking` block.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/anthropic.rs","range":{"start":484,"end":510}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/anthropic_api.rs","range":{"start":211,"end":235}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:cb4b31fc03548066b1872f3d6ae44f09c4a5c620063e8c403a8f51c89763297e","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":36795,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-59","revision":"sha256:2c507eaf813c93ebc0f40d599d9dfbc25279c6444ed3d1c044fb54174f9cf6c1","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-cb4b31fc03548066b1872f3d6ae44f09c4a5c620063e8c403a8f51c89763297e-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Model the remembered reasoning blocks as an enum covering both `thinking { thinking, signature }` and `redacted_thinking { data }`, capture `WireContentBlockStart::RedactedThinking` into `pending_thinking` alongside ordinary thinking, add the matching `WireContentBlock::RedactedThinking` serialization variant, and replay both kinds ahead of the reconstructed `tool_use`. Add a fixture streaming a redacted block before a tool call and asserting it round-trips verbatim on the following request; if replay of redacted blocks is deliberately out of scope, state that limitation explicitly in docs/contracts/anthropic-adapter.md rather than leaving the blanket replay claim.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F5-unbounded-adapter-state","category":"maintainability_issue","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"`tool_use_registry` and `attempt_metadata` grow without bound for the lifetime of the adapter instance","claim":"Both maps are inserted into on every streamed tool call and every completed attempt, and nothing ever removes entries except `cancel`, which drops a single `attempt_metadata` row and never touches `tool_use_registry`. Each registry entry retains the call id, capability name, the fully parsed argument `Value`, and every preceding thinking block's text plus signature — thinking text is frequently the largest part of a turn. An `AnthropicAdapter` held for the life of a daemon and reused across executions therefore accumulates the complete tool-call and reasoning history of every execution it has ever driven, in memory, with no eviction, no per-conversation scoping, and no cap. The contract document notes the registry is adapter-instance-scoped but does not address its lifetime.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/anthropic.rs","range":{"start":100,"end":110}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/anthropic.rs","range":{"start":540,"end":575}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e2e1c0d6b83291d99ee8fa1755f89f52efcd270089766f060699676b9551d918","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":97040,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-59","revision":"sha256:2c507eaf813c93ebc0f40d599d9dfbc25279c6444ed3d1c044fb54174f9cf6c1","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e2e1c0d6b83291d99ee8fa1755f89f52efcd270089766f060699676b9551d918-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Bound both maps — evict a registry entry once its `tool_result` has been replayed, or cap them with an LRU / insertion-ordered ring sized to the largest plausible in-flight turn, and have `cancel` clear the cancelled attempt's registry entries too. Document the resulting lifetime (and the behaviour when an entry has been evicted, which already has a safe fallback path) in docs/contracts/anthropic-adapter.md, so an operator reusing one adapter across many executions knows what is retained.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F1-orphan-tool-result","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"Orphan tool_result with no preceding tool_use block","claim":"Resolved. `push_assistant_and_tool_turn` now has a `None` arm on the registry lookup that synthesizes a `tool_use` block from the `ToolResultPayload` itself (`id: payload.call_id`, `name: payload.capability_name`, `input: {}`) whenever the call id is absent from `tool_use_registry`, so every `tool_result` block is preceded by a `tool_use` of the same id in the same reconstructed assistant turn — including a call refused for malformed arguments and a call id unknown to a fresh adapter instance. The new fixture `refused_malformed_call_never_produces_an_orphan_tool_result_on_the_next_turn` submits the follow-up turn that the previous coverage omitted and asserts, for every `tool_result` block in the request body, that the immediately preceding message is an `assistant` message carrying a `tool_use` with the matching id.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/anthropic.rs","range":{"start":300,"end":330}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:cb4b31fc03548066b1872f3d6ae44f09c4a5c620063e8c403a8f51c89763297e","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":36795,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-59","revision":"sha256:2c507eaf813c93ebc0f40d599d9dfbc25279c6444ed3d1c044fb54174f9cf6c1","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-cb4b31fc03548066b1872f3d6ae44f09c4a5c620063e8c403a8f51c89763297e-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"No further action; the synthesized-tool_use fallback and its regression fixture close the defect.","status":"resolved","supersedes":null}]}
