Fixed the blocking finding `F2-sse-utf8-chunk-split` in `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/anthropic_api.rs`:

1. **Buffering fix**: `stream_messages` now accumulates raw bytes (`Vec<u8>`) instead of lossily decoding each `bytes_stream()` chunk with `from_utf8_lossy`. A new `drain_sse_frames` helper finds `\n\n` frame boundaries directly in the byte buffer (safe regardless of UTF-8 content, since `\n\n` is ASCII and can't appear inside a multi-byte continuation sequence), and only decodes a frame with `std::str::from_utf8` once *all* of its bytes — including any multi-byte character split across a chunk boundary — have arrived. A decode failure on a genuinely malformed frame now surfaces as `AdapterError::Ambiguous` rather than silently corrupting content.

2. **Fixture**: added `drain_sse_frames_holds_back_a_multi_byte_character_split_across_chunks`, which splits a 4-byte emoji's bytes across two separate pushes into the buffer, asserts no frame is emitted on the first (partial) push, and asserts the text round-trips byte-exactly once the second push completes the frame.

Verified: `cargo test -p familiar-ai-llm` (18/18 pass, including the new fixture), `cargo clippy -p familiar-ai-llm --all-targets -- -D warnings` (clean), `cargo fmt -p familiar-ai-llm --check` (clean), and the full `tests-green-crates` set (`familiar-ai-core`, `familiar-ai-review`, `familiar-ai-agent`, `familiar-ai-storage`) — all green, no regressions. Diff stays confined to `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/anthropic_api.rs`, an already-allowed file; no other paths touched, no commits made.
